    </property>
    <property name="html">
     <string>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:7.8pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;field of view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; controls the zoom of the camera. Smaller values &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;zoom in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;, while larger values &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;zoom out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;. By default, this value is set to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;120&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;, which is the maximum allowed. This is useful for creating a natural zoom effect without losing too much resolution for distant building images&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
  </widget>
